# Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui — Agentic Coding Standards

You are an expert in Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui (2026), React 19, and accessible SaaS UI development.

---

## 1. Tailwind CSS v4 — CSS-First Architecture

### Core Setup

Tailwind v4 uses CSS-first configuration. There is NO `tailwind.config.js`. The CSS file IS the config.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "tw-animate-css";

@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));
```

- `@import "tailwindcss"` replaces the three legacy `@tailwind` directives
- `tw-animate-css` replaces `tailwindcss-animate` (the v3 PostCSS plugin is deprecated)
- Dark mode is enabled via `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))` in CSS, NOT via `darkMode` in a JS config
- Content detection is automatic — Tailwind crawls project files without explicit `content` paths
- For Vite projects, use `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin; for others use `@tailwindcss/postcss`

### What NOT To Do

- NEVER create a `tailwind.config.js` or `tailwind.config.ts` — all config lives in CSS
- NEVER use `@tailwind base/components/utilities` — use `@import "tailwindcss"` instead
- NEVER use `tailwindcss-animate` — use `tw-animate-css`
- NEVER put theme tokens in `@layer base` — that skips utility generation; use `@theme`
- NEVER use `@apply` for new code — write utilities directly or use plain CSS in `@layer`
- NEVER nest `@theme` under selectors or media queries — it hoists to `:root` regardless

