## 6. Animation Patterns

### tw-animate-css (shadcn default)

Enter/exit animations for dialogs, dropdowns, and accordions:

```tsx
// Enter
<div className="animate-in fade-in zoom-in-95 duration-200">...</div>

// Exit
<div className="animate-out fade-out zoom-out-95 duration-150">...</div>

// Slide patterns
<div className="animate-in slide-in-from-top-2 fade-in duration-200">...</div>
<div className="animate-in slide-in-from-bottom-4 fade-in duration-300">...</div>
```

Ready-to-use classes: `accordion-down`, `accordion-up`, `collapsible-down`, `collapsible-up`, `caret-blink`

### Custom Animations via @theme

Define custom animations in the CSS `@theme` block:

```css
@theme {
  --animate-shimmer: shimmer 2s linear infinite;
}

@keyframes shimmer {
  0% { background-position: -200% 0; }
  100% { background-position: 200% 0; }
}
```

This generates `animate-shimmer` as a utility class.

### Motion Library (framer-motion / motion)

For complex orchestrated animations, use the `motion` library:

```tsx
import { motion } from "motion/react"

<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  exit={{ opacity: 0, y: -10 }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.2, ease: "easeOut" }}
>
  {children}
</motion.div>
```

### Performance Rules

- Only animate `transform` and `opacity` for GPU-accelerated 60fps rendering
- Avoid animating `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`, `margin`, `padding` — these trigger layout reflow
- Use `will-change-transform` sparingly and only on elements that will actually animate

