## 7. Accessibility

### Focus Management

```tsx
// Keyboard-only focus ring (no ring on mouse click)
<button className="focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-none">

// NEVER remove focus outlines
// WRONG: focus:outline-none (without replacement)
```

### Reduced Motion

ALWAYS respect `prefers-reduced-motion`:

```tsx
// Only animate when safe
<div className="motion-safe:transition-transform motion-safe:duration-300 motion-safe:hover:-translate-y-1 motion-reduce:transition-none">

// Loading spinner with text fallback
<div className="animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none" aria-hidden="true" />
<span className="sr-only motion-reduce:not-sr-only">Loading...</span>
```

Add a global safety net in your base CSS:

```css
@layer base {
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    *, ::before, ::after {
      animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
      transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    }
  }
}
```

### High Contrast and Forced Colors

```tsx
// Adapt to contrast preferences
<button className="border-border contrast-more:border-foreground">

// Windows High Contrast Mode
<div className="forced-colors:bg-[Highlight] forced-colors:text-[HighlightText]">
```

```css
@media (forced-colors: active) {
  :focus-visible {
    outline-color: Highlight;
  }
}
```

### Color Contrast Requirements (WCAG 2.2)

- Normal text: minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio
- Large text (18px+ bold, 24px+ regular): minimum 3:1
- UI components and graphical objects: minimum 3:1
- Verify `muted-foreground` meets 4.5:1 on card/muted backgrounds, not just white

### Required ARIA Patterns

- Icon-only buttons MUST have `aria-label` or contain `<span className="sr-only">`
- All form inputs MUST have associated `<label>` elements or `aria-label`
- Use semantic landmarks: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<footer>`
- Include skip-to-content link for keyboard navigation
- Images must have `alt` text (empty `alt=""` for decorative images)
- Use `aria-live="polite"` for dynamic content updates (toasts, status messages)

