## 9. CSS Best Practices

### Global Styles (`globals.css`)

The complete structure of a Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui globals.css:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "tw-animate-css";

@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));

@theme inline {
  /* Radius tokens */
  --radius-sm: calc(var(--radius) - 4px);
  --radius-md: calc(var(--radius) - 2px);
  --radius-lg: var(--radius);
  --radius-xl: calc(var(--radius) + 4px);

  /* Color token mappings */
  --color-background: var(--background);
  --color-foreground: var(--foreground);
  /* ... all semantic tokens ... */
}

:root {
  --radius: 0.625rem;
  --background: oklch(1 0 0);
  --foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
  /* ... all light mode values ... */
}

.dark {
  --background: oklch(0.145 0 0);
  --foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
  /* ... all dark mode values ... */
}

@layer base {
  * {
    @apply border-border;
  }
  body {
    @apply bg-background text-foreground;
  }
  :focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--ring);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  html {
    scrollbar-gutter: stable;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    *, ::before, ::after {
      animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
      transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    }
  }
  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    :focus-visible {
      outline-color: Highlight;
    }
  }
}
```

### Referencing Tokens in Custom CSS

Because `@theme` writes tokens to `:root` as CSS custom properties, custom CSS reads them directly:

```css
.prose blockquote {
  border-left: 4px solid var(--border);
  color: var(--muted-foreground);
}
```

### What NOT To Do in CSS

- NEVER define colors with `@theme inline` when they need dark mode switching
- NEVER scatter arbitrary values (`bg-[#1a2b3c]`) — tokenize everything
- NEVER remove focus styles with `:focus { outline: none }` — use `:focus-visible` for keyboard-only rings
- NEVER use `@apply` in new code for simple class composition — write utilities directly
- NEVER import `tailwindcss-animate` — use `tw-animate-css`
- NEVER duplicate the `@tailwindcss/postcss` plugin with the `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin

