## 10. shadcn/ui Project Configuration

### `components.json` Key Settings

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema.json",
  "style": "new-york",
  "tailwind": {
    "config": "",
    "css": "src/app/globals.css",
    "baseColor": "neutral",
    "cssVariables": true
  },
  "aliases": {
    "components": "@/components",
    "ui": "@/components/ui",
    "utils": "@/lib/utils",
    "hooks": "@/hooks",
    "lib": "@/lib"
  }
}
```

- `style`: always `"new-york"` (default is deprecated)
- `tailwind.config`: leave empty string `""` for v4 (no JS config)
- `cssVariables`: MUST be `true` — enables semantic token theming
- `baseColor`: `"neutral"`, `"stone"`, `"zinc"`, `"mauve"`, `"olive"`, `"mist"`, or `"taupe"`

### shadcn/skills Integration

Generate the skills file for AI agent context:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest skills generate   # Creates .shadcn/skills.md
npx shadcn@latest skills update     # Refresh after adding components
npx shadcn@latest skills check      # Validate setup
```

Reference the skills file in your project's AI context (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, or cursor rules).

### MCP Server for Agent Workflows

```bash
npx shadcn@latest mcp init --client cursor
```

This enables agents to search, preview, and install components from natural language via the shadcn MCP server. Config lives in `.cursor/mcp.json`.

